# Adverbs (%include'd from en.gram).
#
# A closed list of manner adverbs for now. Productive -ly derivation is a later
# slice: it would need adverb-forming adjectives (quick, slow, loud, ...) and the
# -ly spelling rules, and naive -ly over the current adjective set would
# over-generate (*bigly, *oldly). Adverbs don't inflect or agree, so they carry
# no features; they're transparent to subject-verb agreement (a modified VP keeps
# its head verb's features).
loudly  : Adv
quickly : Adv
slowly  : Adv
quietly : Adv
well    : Adv
badly   : Adv
